Read this before using the software. If you use it, you accept these terms.


1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means SheetSmith, in source or built form, together with its
   documentation, as published by the Licensor.

   "Licensor" means Misha Stoyanov, the author and sole copyright holder.

   "You" means the individual or organisation exercising the rights below. For an
   organisation, "you" includes every entity that controls it, is controlled by
   it, or is under common control with it.

   "Unmodified" means byte-for-byte as published by the Licensor. Supplying
   configuration through the means the Software itself provides — environment
   variables, settings files, values entered in its own interface, the choice of
   language model, the contents of your spreadsheets — is not a modification.

   "Third Party" means anyone other than you, your employees, and your
   contractors acting for you.


2. WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING, AT NO CHARGE

   a) Run the Software, Unmodified, on hardware you own or control, or on
      private infrastructure you rent for your own use. This applies equally to a
      person on one machine and to a company across its whole staff. No fee, no
      registration, no notice to the Licensor.

      Your own work may be commercial. A company may run it on its own business,
      and you may use it as a tool in work you are paid for — tidying a client's
      spreadsheet and invoicing for your time is your business, and the Software
      is no more part of that bargain than the computer you ran it on.

      What this does not grant is earning money from the Software itself. That is
      section 3(a), and the distinction is the whole point: use it to do your
      work, do not make it the product you sell.

   b) Read, study, and analyse the source.

   c) Make and keep verbatim copies of the Software, and give verbatim copies to
      others, provided every copy keeps this license and all copyright notices
      intact, and provided you charge nothing for the copy itself.


