   The rights in this section are reserved. They are not granted by this license,
   they are not granted by implication, and they do not become available with the
   passage of time. Each is available on terms agreed with the Licensor, who
   built this software and decides what it costs.

   a) HOSTING, AND MAKING MONEY FROM IT. Making the Software, or any service
      built on it, available to a Third Party over a network — as a hosted
      product, a paid or unpaid service, an internal offering to another
      organisation, or any other arrangement in which a Third Party uses an
      instance you operate. Whether you charge for it makes no difference: a free
      public instance needs an agreement exactly as a paid one does. Your own
      staff are not a Third Party, so running one instance for your whole company
      is section 2(a) and needs no agreement.

      Equally reserved is deriving revenue from the Software by any means,
      including from an instance offered at no charge: subscription or per-use
      fees, advertising of any kind, sponsorship, affiliate or referral
      arrangements, selling data gathered through it, and bundling it into
      something else you sell. Advertising is named because "it is free to the
      user" is not the same as "nobody is being paid".

   b) MODIFICATION. Altering, adapting, translating, extending, or building upon
      the Software, or combining it with other software so as to create a
      derivative work. This includes adding features, changing behaviour, and
      removing parts. The single exception is section 4.

   c) REDISTRIBUTION OF CHANGES. Distributing, publishing, or otherwise supplying
      to anyone a version of the Software that is not Unmodified.

   d) Removing, obscuring, or altering this license, the copyright notices, or
      the attribution the Software displays.

   To ask about any of these, open an issue at
   https://github.com/MishaStoyanov/sheetsmith or contact the Licensor directly.


